From e627b81d562e6b8191b70cf14d01e0791c16374a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:01:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: qcom: gpi: Clear the peripheral configuration on
 release

The GPI channel survives dma_release_channel(), but its peripheral
configuration does not. Leaving the freed pointer in the channel
lets the next client pass it to krealloc() or free it a second time.
On the Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro, rebinding the GENI SPI controller can then
leave the Novatek touchscreen with a corrupted transfer and no input.

Clear the configuration pointer when freeing it so the next client
allocates its own configuration.

Fixes: 5d0c3533a19f ("dmaengine: qcom: Add GPI dma driver")
---
 drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c b/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
index a5055a6273af..abf7a7e7bfee 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
@@ -2011,6 +2011,7 @@ static void gpi_free_chan_resources(struct dma_chan *chan)
 	gpi_free_ring(&gchan->ch_ring, gpii);
 	vchan_free_chan_resources(&gchan->vc);
 	kfree(gchan->config);
+	gchan->config = NULL;
 
 	write_lock_irq(&gpii->pm_lock);
 	gchan->pm_state = DISABLE_STATE;
